# One checkout, the same bytes on every platform.
#
# Windows checks out files with CRLF by default, which makes a diff of "the same" file show
# every line as changed, and turns any byte-for-byte comparison of a checked-in file into a
# platform-dependent answer. Open Download Manager ships to all three platforms, so the working tree is
# pinned to LF everywhere and the platform difference is confined to binaries.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.exe binary
*.png binary
